\n\n1. For INITIAL SETUP of a brand new Mac Mini - you DO need a monitor, keyboard, and mouse to go through macOS Setup Assistant (language, Wi-Fi, Apple ID, etc.). You can't skip this.\nAfter setup, though, it can run fully headless via Screen Sharing/Remote Login over that same Thunderbolt connection. There might be workarounds like Apple Configurator for the initial setup step, but I should double-check whether a MacBook's screen can actually double as an external display for the Mini over Thunderbolt — I don't think Macs support acting as displays for other Macs that way."}
