alone takes ~30-40GB. After apps + files, you'll have ~150GB left |\n| **512GB** ✅ | Most people. Apps, photos, some video editing | **Best value for most users** |\n| **1TB** | Video editing, big projects, AI models, lots of media | Expensive but comfortable |\n| **2TB** | Professional video/photo work | Only if you REALLY need it |\n\n> [!IMPORTANT]\n> **You CANNOT upgrade storage later.** It's soldered like the RAM. Pick the right size now or you'll be stuck using external drives forever.\n\n---\n\n## 🏆 My Recommendation For You\n\n**Mac Mini M4 — 32GB RAM / 512GB SSD → ~₹99,900**\n\nThis gives you:\n- ✅ 32GB RAM (double your MacBook's 16GB)\n- ✅ 512GB storage (comfortable for most work)\n- ✅ Can run headless connected to your MacBook via Thunderbolt\n- ✅ Cheapest 32GB Mac you can buy anywhere\n\n**Exact prices change with sales — always check [apple.com/in](https://www.apple.com/in/shop/buy-mac/mac-mini) for the latest.**"}
